@startuml

start

:Thermal management controller operates as state machine within RTOS;

fork
  :Govern PWM fans;
fork again
  :Govern liquid-cooling loops using multi-threaded architecture;
end fork

:High-priority ISR triggered by PMIC/dedicated temperature sensors;
if (Abnormal temperature rise?) then (yes)
  :Initiate safety protocols;

  :Employ primary control loop;
  if (Early warning threshold reached?) then (yes)
    :Spawn concurrent tasks from priority queue;
    :Actively monitor temperature in fixed cycles;
    if (Thermal stability confirmed?) then (yes)
      :Cease;
    else (no)
      :Escalate;
    end if
  else (no)
  end if

  if(Temperature remains < threshold but exhibits significant fluctuation?) then(yes)
    :Lower-priority task logs anomaly to structured audit trail in ring buffer protected by mutex;
  else(no)
  end if
else (no)
end if

  :All critical safety actions verified;
  fork
    :Sensor fusion;
  fork again
    :Calibration routines;
  fork again
    :Redundancy management for out-of-range readings;
  end fork

  :Processing results and audit logs asynchronously flushed to non-volatile memory under strict I/O budget constraints;

:Dedicated watchdog timer supervises entire sequence;
:Ensure failsafe, controlled cool-down path is executed if required;

stop

@enduml
